WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.630
On the eastern slopes of
the Andes, in northern Peru,

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:06.610
villages are scattered across steep land.

3
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:09.670
This is among the least
developed parts of Peru.

4
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.010
Few people had grid electricity.

5
00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:14.670
But high rainfall feeds many streams.

6
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.130
And a stream can turn a turbine.

7
00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:21.110
In one village, people who
had left began to move back.

8
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:24.110
Why would a stream's
electricity bring them home?

9
00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:27.630
In this mission, you'll find out
what makes up a carbon footprint,

10
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:32.490
and ways to save energy at
home, at work and on the move.

11
00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:35.690
Then you'll follow water
through a micro-hydro scheme,

12
00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:38.590
from canal to turbine to village.

13
00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:43.470
Your mission: explain why people who
had left this Andean village moved back.
